  "answer_text": "Yes. Cato supports IPv6-only branch sites. The Cato Client supports last-mile IPv6-only connections (with NAT64 to translate IPv6 addresses to IPv4 for the Cato Cloud). Socket sites can operate with IPv6-only Internet connectivity (IPv6-only WAN) using IPv4-over-IPv6 mechanisms as needed. Roadmap details with dates for next year are not available in the knowledge base.",
